    session_summary: "This summary captures the state of the analysis for \"La Soluci\303\263n\" (Quantum OS). The discovery phase is complete, and the next agent should proceed directly to generating the requested clinical report.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **360-Degree Scientific and Technical Analysis:** The user requested an exhaustive analysis of the application across 12 specific disciplines (Engineering, UI/UX, Game Design, Psychology, etc.).\n  - **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION (Drafting the report).\n  - **Requirement:** Generate a clinical report containing:\n    1.  **Diagn\303\263stico Multidisciplinario:** Critical findings from the 12 perspectives.\n    2.  **Matriz de Prioridades:** A Markdown table classifying issues (Critical/Medium/Low) and their source.\n    3.  **Protocolo de Intervenci\303\263n (Roadmap):** 3 actionable code-based steps to elevate the platform.\n- **Constraint:** Do not generate code until the analysis report is complete.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Project Identity:** \"La Soluci\303\263n\" (Quantum OS) is a gamified productivity platform with a Sci-Fi/Solo Leveling aesthetic.\n- **Core Philosophy:** High-performance habits, Pomodoro-based deep work, and \"Zero Friction\" interaction.\n- **Key Features:** RPG leveling system (XP/HP/Coins), \"Oracle\" AI assistant, Smart Recall, and daily boss encounters.\n- **Scope:** The user expects a high-level, \"Silicon Valley\" standard of engineering and design.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Discovery Phase:** Completed a full architectural audit of the codebase.\n- **Mapping:**\n  - **State Management:** Mapped the flow between `usePlayerStore`, `useTaskStore`, `useUIStore`, and `useAppStore`.\n  - **Business Logic:** Analyzed `gameEngine.ts` as the central controller for game state transitions, rewards, and task management.\n  - **Persistence:** Audited `storage.ts` and its interaction with LocalStorage and Firebase synchronization.\n  - **UI/UX:** Reviewed `AppLayout.tsx` and `PomodoroTimer.tsx` to understand the component hierarchy and \"juice\" (visual feedback) implementation.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:** The app uses a decoupled state management approach via Zustand. `gameEngine.ts` acts as the primary service layer, importing stores to execute logic.\n- **Data Flow:** `storage.ts` provides a safety layer for LocalStorage (handling potential iframe/sandbox issues). Firebase is used for cloud sync, but the app is designed to be functional offline.\n- **Coupling:** `gameEngine.ts` is highly coupled with the stores. It directly triggers UI state changes (modals, floating effects) and updates player/task state.\n- **Constraints:** The app relies on `canvas-confetti` for rewards and `motion` (framer-motion) for animations. The aesthetic is heavily dependent on CSS variables defined in `index.css` (e.g., `scifi-glass-panel`).\n- **Dependencies:** The project uses `@google/genai` for AI features and `vite-plugin-pwa` for offline capabilities.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:** None.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/types.ts`: Core type definitions for the game (PlayerStats, TaskItem, etc.).\n  - `/src/store/usePlayerStore.ts`: Central store for player stats and RPG logic.\n  - `/src/utils/storage.ts`: Persistence layer and migration logic.\n  - `/src/components/AppLayout.tsx`: Main UI orchestration and layout.\n  - `/src/engine/gameEngine.ts`: The \"brain\" of the app; handles all game-state mutations and side effects.\n  - `/src/components/PomodoroTimer.tsx`: Example of a specialized feature component with its own state and sound integration.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Immediate Task:** Generate the 3-part Clinical Report (Diagn\303\263stico, Matriz, Roadmap) as requested by the user.\n- **Next Steps for the Next Agent:**\n  1.  Synthesize the findings from the 12 perspectives into the required report format.\n  2.  Ensure the \"Matriz de Prioridades\" includes specific components (e.g., `gameEngine.ts` coupling, state consistency in `usePlayerStore.ts`).\n  3.  Propose the 3-step roadmap based on the identified architectural bottlenecks.\n- **Relevant Files for Report Generation:** All viewed files listed in Section 5 are critical for the analysis. No further discovery is required."
