afely apply.\n\n\n**Implementing the Changes**\n\nI\'ve decided to act now and apply all the safe code changes. I am reviewing the list of changes I designed and executed: streamlining state management with Zustand for player experience and task logic, introducing a persistent timer for the Deep Work mode, and centralizing UI elements within `useUIStore` to better manage pop-ups and notifications, and an update to reduce the penalty for failure. I\'ll provide an overview of my process.\n\n\n**Applying Visual Adjustments**\n\nI\'ve just applied a visual tweak. Following the request, I\'ve updated the base CSS (`src/index.css`) by changing the background from pure black (`#000000`) to a darker shade, `#030712`, to reduce eye strain, a quick win as it was a small change. I\'m also preparing to apply changes to `takeDamage` for the soft penalty. I\'ll provide an explanation of my action.\n\n\n**Summarizing Key Refactors**\n\nI\'ve crafted a professional, concise summary of the architectural refactoring, based on my previous analysis. I\'ve focused on these four key improvements: I refactored state management and the penalty system using Zustand, moving complex logic from `gameEngine` into stores for players and tasks. I also introduced a \"soft penalty,\" limiting losses to protect user retention. I then re-wrote the Pomodoro logic so that the timer persists through page reloads, and silence interuptions while in deep work mode. I implemented a queue for notifications and pop-ups within a dedicated UI store.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve just applied a visual tweak, changing the background in `src/index.css` from pure black to a slightly less harsh dark tone (`#030712`) to reduce eye strain. I\'ve also refactored the UI so that pop-ups and notifications are now displayed within the application flow. I\'m moving on to review the changes in `usePlayerStore.ts` before summarizing.\n\n\n**Applying UI Adjustments**\n\nI\'ve just applied a quick visual enhancement to `src/index.css` by changing the background color to a darker tone (`#030712`) to reduce eye strain. I\'ve also implemented a \"soft penalty\" in `src/store/usePlayerStore.ts`, limiting XP and coins lost on failure. I\'m focusing on providing the user with a concise summary of my actions, bearing in mind the user\'s intent to receive a straightforward overview.\n\n\n"
