    thinking: "**Examining App Initialization**\n\nI\'ve taken a look at `App.tsx` - it seems quite straightforward. Now I\'m checking `src/engine/gameEngine.ts` to see how `generateDailyTasks` is called, in case we need to leverage an initialization hook instead. I\'m also considering persisting the task store data.\n\n\n**Analyzing Sync Mechanisms**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the sync mechanisms, and it appears that the current implementation in `useCloudSync.ts` already addresses immediate Zustand updates followed by debounced saves to Firestore. The debounced `useEffect` handles this nicely, aligning with the requirement for immediate state impact and background syncing. Now, I\'m verifying the re-attempt logic during connection loss within `useCloudSync.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Sync Queue**\n\nI\'m now implementing a `syncQueue` wrapper within `useCloudSync.ts`. The initial plan was to create a background sync queue, but I realized Firestore\'s `writeBatch` combined with the persistent local cache already functions as one! However, the user might want explicit retry logic for the `performSave` function if network errors occur during `commit()`. So, I\'m now making a robust wrapper for it, focusing on ensuring that the app works in all scenarios.\n\n\n"
