  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the data structure. Player stats are straightforward, going directly under the user ID. Tasks, Pomodoro sessions, custom habits, and shop rewards each get their own sub-collections within the user\'s data, with unique IDs for each item within those collections. This seems like a scalable starting point.\n\n\n**Refining Security Rules**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Firestore security rules. My focus is crafting robust rules to protect data integrity. Specifically, I\'m setting up checks to prevent unreasonable updates to `currentXp` and `coins`, implementing delta limits, and ensuring type validation (no string XP!). I\'m also including helper functions for authentication and ownership checks.\n\n\n**Strengthening Access Controls**\n\nI\'ve significantly tightened the security rules. I\'m focusing on user documents and sub-collections, specifically, player stats. There are now strict rules for `currentXp` and `coins`, ensuring data type validation and delta limits on updates to prevent abuse; there\'s a cap of 5000 units per sync to prevent exploits. I\'ve also integrated helper functions for authentication and ownership checks, providing a robust, scalable security approach.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 726023453
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
