    thinking: "**Considering Implementation Strategies**\n\nI\'m exploring the best way to handle `systemEntropy`. I\'m leaning toward either adding a `systemEntropy` field directly to `PlayerStats`, or extending the Zustand store to house it. I\'m also checking if adding it to `PlayerStats` causes any TS issues. I\'m trying to find where `PlayerStats` is defined for maximum clarity.\n\n\n**Adding System Entropy**\n\nOkay, great news! I\'ve confirmed we can easily add `systemEntropy?: number;` to the `PlayerStats` interface within `/src/types.ts`. I\'ve located the appropriate line, it\'s 115, and the change seems straightforward. Now, the next step is designing the mechanics for how this deterministic entropy should fluctuate. I\'m brainstorming a fun and immersive system, focusing on pending/completed tasks and the passage of time to dynamically adjust the entropy level.\n\n\n**Formulating Entropy Calculation**\n\nI\'ve crafted a deterministic formula for `systemEntropy` based on time and task completion. The formula utilizes the current hour (normalized) and the ratio of incomplete to total tasks. Time adds up to 40% to entropy, and each incomplete task adds 60% (scaled). This results in a value between 0 and 100, which is then capped appropriately. It\'s a clean, logical approach!\n\n\n"
