    thinking: "**Developing Quantum Soundscape**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component breakdown for the \"Quantum Soundscape\" engine. My focus is on determining the necessary states and elements. I want to build a hybrid procedural engine as \"Opci\303\263n 3\", so I want to build out a more flexible solution.\n\n\n**Defining Audio Channels**\n\nI\'ve specified the foundational structure of the audio engine within `quantumSoundscape.ts`. I\'m starting by defining two primary audio channels. The first channel, \"Base de Aislamiento,\" will feature algorithmic noise generation: brown, pink, and white noise with independent volume control. The second is for binaural beats, \"Pulsos Binaurales Neuro-modulados,\" using a carrier frequency and a stereo split with configurable frequency deltas, including options for Gamma, Beta, Alpha, and Theta brainwave states.\n\n\n**Expanding Audio Architecture**\n\nI\'ve just added a third channel, \"Drone Atmosf\303\251rico Sci-Fi Procedural,\" which will simulate spacecraft interiors or quantum reactor sounds. It uses a low-frequency carrier modulated by a sub-bass oscillator and a subtle LFO for that characteristic, breathing effect. Stereo detuning adds to the spatial depth. I\'ve also implemented master controls for volume, power, smooth fade-in/out, and a Tibetan bell chime.\n\n\n"
