  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Foundation**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the architecture\'s modularity. Now, I\'m diving into designing `src/utils/quantumSoundscape.ts`. My initial focus is on the engine features: the Web Audio Context initialization on user interaction. The core architecture will encompass a Master Gain, followed by a gentle smoothing filter, leading to the destination. Channel 1 will be...\n\n\n**Implementing Noise Generation**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress implementing the noise generation. I\'ve got procedural `AudioBuffer`s for brown, pink, and white noise. Brown noise integrates a white noise filter, and a 2nd order BiquadFilter. Pink uses Paul Kellett\'s algorithm followed by bandpass. White noise has a gentle ceiling. Now I\'m working on Channel 1\'s gain node.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Constructing Binaural Beats**\n\nI\'m now deep into designing Channel 2, which will focus on binaural beats. I\'m building it with a ChannelMergerNode, merging a left and right oscillator. I\'ve established a 216 Hz carrier frequency as a base. I\'m implementing frequency modes: gamma, beta, alpha, and theta. I\'ll cap off the implementation by including lowpass filters on the oscillators to eliminate potentially disruptive harmonics.\n\n\n**Expanding the Soundscape**\n\nI\'m now integrating Channel 3, the drone atmosf\303\251r\303\255co, with its low sine wave carrier, detuned fifth, and LFO modulation. It\'s designed to breathe rhythmically, mimicking a spacecraft\'s core. I\'m focusing on stereo panning for a spatial effect, followed by the Channel 3 gain node. Then, I\'m defining master functions for the soundscape\'s control and state.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 807665957
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
